{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00362",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.77,
      "end_seconds": 5.53,
      "duration_seconds": 4.76,
      "text": "All set here, doctor. Chart's updated, and I'll read the readings out when you're ready."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.36,
      "end_seconds": 10.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.71,
      "text": "Thanks. Hello, come in, sit down. What brings you in today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 11.35,
      "end_seconds": 14.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "Thank you for fitting us in, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 14.97,
      "end_seconds": 19.31,
      "duration_seconds": 4.34,
      "text": "So the thing is, I've got a very sore throat."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 19.77,
      "end_seconds": 21.74,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "When did you first notice it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 22.92,
      "end_seconds": 25.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "It's been about a week now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.04,
      "end_seconds": 39.28,
      "duration_seconds": 10.24,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse. I'll explain everything as we go along."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.78,
      "end_seconds": 55.33,
      "duration_seconds": 14.55,
      "text": "Pretty severe, if I'm being honest. Swallowing definitely sets it off. I've had pain on swallowing too, for two weeks. About pain on swallowing, it's all the time. A fever was there, but it's gone away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 56.36,
      "end_seconds": 59.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "Do you have everything you need to get home alright?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 61.04,
      "end_seconds": 73.17,
      "duration_seconds": 12.13,
      "text": "Yes, I've got my transport sorted. It's a bit of a trek, but I'm used to the journey by now, and I brought something to read for the wait."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 73.8,
      "end_seconds": 76.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "Have you had any difficulty breathing or ear pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 77.43,
      "end_seconds": 78.98,
      "duration_seconds": 1.55,
      "text": "No, none of those."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.1,
      "end_seconds": 83.65,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "Have you had any cough, runny nose or rash?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.52,
      "end_seconds": 88.65,
      "duration_seconds": 4.13,
      "text": "I haven't had cough, runny nose or rash, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.09,
      "end_seconds": 91.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "Anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 92.13,
      "end_seconds": 93.37,
      "duration_seconds": 1.24,
      "text": "Nothing there, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.2,
      "end_seconds": 97.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "How about your heart, any problems like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.69,
      "end_seconds": 99.57,
      "duration_seconds": 1.88,
      "text": "No, that's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.19,
      "end_seconds": 112.59,
      "duration_seconds": 12.4,
      "text": "Just so you know how the rest of the visit will go: I'll finish my notes, we'll agree on the plan, and the front desk will help with anything that needs booking. You shouldn't need to chase anything yourself."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 113.42,
      "end_seconds": 116.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "Good, I was wondering how this would go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 117.38,
      "end_seconds": 130.25,
      "duration_seconds": 12.87,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. BMI works out to 22.2, blood pressure 118 over 66, respiratory rate 22. Weight 59 kilos, temperature is 38.2 degrees, saturation 95 percent, height 163 centimetres, heart rate 97."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.91,
      "end_seconds": 136.77,
      "duration_seconds": 5.86,
      "text": "Good, thank you. Is there anyone at home who can help you out if you need it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 137.58,
      "end_seconds": 148.27,
      "duration_seconds": 10.69,
      "text": "So, yes, there's family around most evenings, and they've been very good about checking in, although they do worry more than they need to."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 151.9,
      "end_seconds": 156.01,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "What about your general health, any conditions you're being treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 157.03,
      "end_seconds": 173.98,
      "duration_seconds": 16.95,
      "text": "I've got asthma. A neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it. I've got acid reflux. Thin bones, for five years. I took the morning off to come in today. I've never really been one for hospitals."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.77,
      "end_seconds": 175.75,
      "duration_seconds": 0.98,
      "text": "Okay. Anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.43,
      "end_seconds": 183.61,
      "duration_seconds": 7.18,
      "text": "Okay, thin bones, that's already on your record. Good to know. What about allergies, to medicines or foods or anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 184.23,
      "end_seconds": 186.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Right, not that I know, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 187.75,
      "end_seconds": 191.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "Have you been able to keep up with your usual activities?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 192.77,
      "end_seconds": 205.04,
      "duration_seconds": 12.27,
      "text": "For the most part, yes. I just carry on and try not to dwell on things too much, though I won't pretend it hasn't crossed my mind a few times."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.22,
      "end_seconds": 211.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "What medicines do you take regularly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 215.0,
      "end_seconds": 222.24,
      "duration_seconds": 7.24,
      "text": "Asthalin inhaler, when needed for my asthma. My sister suggested writing things down, but I forgot."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.47,
      "end_seconds": 226.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "How long have you been on it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 227.42,
      "end_seconds": 231.96,
      "duration_seconds": 4.54,
      "text": "For about a month. Omeprazole, 20 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 232.81,
      "end_seconds": 237.27,
      "duration_seconds": 4.46,
      "text": "Doctor, our chart from the last visit lists it as 10 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.06,
      "end_seconds": 241.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "Hm. Do you have the latest prescription with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 242.08,
      "end_seconds": 244.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "No, I left it at home."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 245.36,
      "end_seconds": 250.28,
      "duration_seconds": 4.92,
      "text": "So, what about family history, any illnesses that run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 251.19,
      "end_seconds": 253.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "My father had a heart attack."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 254.55,
      "end_seconds": 257.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "Are you comfortable? Do you want some water?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 257.36,
      "end_seconds": 260.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "Yes, some water would be nice, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.16,
      "end_seconds": 264.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "Let me make a quick note of that before I forget."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 265.34,
      "end_seconds": 266.04,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.87,
      "end_seconds": 300.28,
      "duration_seconds": 20.41,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. Okay, so my impression from what you've said is this: My working impression is tonsillitis, probably bacterial. I'd also keep a viral throat infection in mind. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had a very sore throat for about a week, severe, and no runny nose or rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 300.63,
      "end_seconds": 302.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "Exactly, that's what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 303.24,
      "end_seconds": 307.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "Is there anything you were hoping to get out of today's visit?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 308.61,
      "end_seconds": 312.39,
      "duration_seconds": 3.78,
      "text": "Mostly I just want to understand what's going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 313.77,
      "end_seconds": 341.13,
      "duration_seconds": 27.36,
      "text": "I'm going to order a throat swab, for sore throat. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture. Let's use paracetamol, 500 milligrams, every six hours if needed, for three days. That should help with fever and body aches. The pharmacy will go through the details again when you pick it up. Finish the whole course of antibiotics even if you feel better after two days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 342.62,
      "end_seconds": 361.32,
      "duration_seconds": 18.7,
      "text": "A short walk every day, even twenty minutes, will help more than you'd think. Make sure you're drinking plenty of fluids, two to three litres a day if you can, and get proper rest. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 361.74,
      "end_seconds": 363.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.41,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 364.72,
      "end_seconds": 375.61,
      "duration_seconds": 10.89,
      "text": "Please don't sit on it if you can't swallow your saliva or you have trouble breathing. That's the point to get seen urgently. Come back if it's not better in three days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 376.44,
      "end_seconds": 377.14,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 378.51,
      "end_seconds": 384.09,
      "duration_seconds": 5.58,
      "text": "I want to be sure we're on the same page. How would you describe the plan?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 385.27,
      "end_seconds": 396.51,
      "duration_seconds": 11.24,
      "text": "So, I take the paracetamol, 500 milligrams, every six hours if needed and come back if it's not better in three days. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 397.61,
      "end_seconds": 402.19,
      "duration_seconds": 4.58,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Take care, and don't hesitate to call if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 403.59,
      "end_seconds": 406.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "Nothing more from me, doctor, thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 407.49,
      "end_seconds": 408.27,
      "duration_seconds": 0.78,
      "text": "Take care."
    }
  ]
}